    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d213">

                <pb facs="0294" n="282" xml:id="pg282"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">390.1115A/1010b: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Consul General at
                        Calcutta</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Schnare</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1942-07-24T14:00:00-04:00">July 24, 1942—2 p.m.</date></dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>318. Your 506, July 14. Department informed two large vessels operating under War
                    Shipping Administration presently available at Karachi for evacuation purposes.
                    Available accommodations on these vessels apparently ample to afford all persons
                    referred to in your 506 opportunity of repatriation.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Hull</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
